Make the eMMC write path detect and retry a silently lost block.

TC is treated as success today, but the card's CRC status for the last block
can arrive after TC, and nothing waits for DAT0 to go idle.  A bad write then
looks fine and the block is lost - matching the HFS "BlockMarkFreeInternal()
trying to free unallocated blocks on volume iOSRoot <524257,1>" +
hfs_mark_inconsistent flood, which in turn breaks containermanagerd's SQLite
container database (ContainerManagerCommon +0x8e83c, brk #1).

 1. After TC: wait DAT0 idle, re-check the INT error bits (DCRC/AC12/DRTO);
    a set bit fails the block and oe_write_lba() retries it.
 2. emmcroot_wrverify=1: read every written block back and compare, printing
    "ONC EMMC: wrverify mismatch lba=0x..." on a silent loss (off by default).

Base: bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c from CI main after 0118, saved as
tmp/onc_emmc_after_0119.c.  Only bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c changes.
--- a/bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/onc_emmc.c
@@ -242,6 +242,7 @@
 	bool nobranch;		/* emmcroot_nobranch=1: skip the GCC branch kick */
 	bool kick_always;	/* emmcroot_kickalways=1: old kick-per-command */
 	bool force_kick;	/* next command must kick the branch */
+	bool wr_verify;		/* emmcroot_wrverify=1: read back every write */
 	uint64_t last_cmd_end;	/* timestamp of the previous command end */
 } oe;
 
@@ -1067,6 +1068,38 @@
 	rc = oe_wait_int(OE_INT_TC, OE_DATA_TIMEOUT_NS, &st);
 	if (rc != 0) {
 		goto out;
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The card reports the block's CRC status after the data phase, and the
+	 * controller can raise TC before that status is available: a bad write
+	 * then looks successful and the block is lost silently.  On this phone
+	 * that surfaced as the HFS flood
+	 *   "hfs: BlockMarkFreeInternal() trying to free unallocated blocks
+	 *    on volume iOSRoot <524257,1>" + hfs_mark_inconsistent,
+	 * which in turn broke containermanagerd's SQLite container database.
+	 * So wait for DAT0 to go idle, look at the error bits once more, and
+	 * optionally read the block back and compare.
+	 */
+	(void)oe_wait_dat_idle(OE_DAT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_NS);
+	{
+		uint32_t est = oe_rd(oe.hc, R_INT);
+
+		if ((est & OE_INT_ERR) != 0) {
+			st = est;
+			rc = EIO;
+			goto out;
+		}
+	}
+	if (oe.wr_verify) {
+		uint8_t back[OE_BLOCK_SIZE];
+
+		if (oe_read_lba(arg, back) != 0 ||
+		    memcmp(back, in, OE_BLOCK_SIZE) != 0) {
+			printf("ONC EMMC: wrverify mismatch lba=0x%x\n", arg);
+			rc = EIO;
+			goto out;
+		}
 	}
 
 out:
@@ -2099,6 +2132,10 @@
 			PE_parse_boot_argn("emmcroot_kickalways", &nobr,
 			    sizeof(nobr));
 			oe.kick_always = (nobr != 0);
+			nobr = 0;
+			PE_parse_boot_argn("emmcroot_wrverify", &nobr,
+			    sizeof(nobr));
+			oe.wr_verify = (nobr != 0);
 		}
 	}
 	{
